<section>
  <h2>Applied Research Focus</h2>
  <p>Keystone Neuroinformatics supports work at the intersection of psychiatry, behavioral health informatics, clinical AI evaluation, computational psychiatry, neuroimaging, digital phenotyping, and translational data science. The site outlines practical service areas for research groups, digital health teams, clinical collaborators, and technical organizations, and translates those services into projects, publications, or workflow implementation.</p>
</section>

<section>
  <h2>Professional foundation</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Clinical psychiatry with emphasis on neuropsychiatric and complex behavioral health conditions.</li>
    <li>Translational research spanning neuroimaging, computational psychiatry, and intervention studies.</li>
    <li>Clinical trial experience in mood disorders and related psychiatric therapeutics.</li>
    <li>Recent work in AI model evaluation, medical reasoning assessment, and clinically informed AI development.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section>
  <h2>What ties the work together</h2>
  <p>The through-line is practical translation: using computation, imaging, trial methods, and AI evaluation to address clinically meaningful questions in psychiatry and behavioral health. Those same themes shape the project pages and the research archive on this site.</p>
</section>

<section class="callout">
  <h2>Publication-backed direction</h2>
  <p>The site prioritizes concise summaries of published work, a small number of coherent project areas, and a clean structure for future additions rather than a broad list of disconnected interests.</p>
</section>
